# Audit report -- Phase 275: one definition of the audit verdict

**Verdict**: PASS
**Target**: docs/plan-qor-phase275-one-verdict-definition.md (iteration 6)
**Session**: 2026-09-08T1303-1f0903
**Issues**: GH #424, GH #462
**Mode**: adversarial; six review rounds, independent reviewer, 19 findings all reproduced by the author before acceptance
**Iterations**: 6 (iterations 1-5 VETOed)

## Scope

Covers a shared dialect owning the audit report's verdict and target fields, consumed by `intent_lock` and `verdict_reconcile`. Both gates read the same file and disagreed about its verdict on 44% of real reports: one failing open, one failing closed on valid input. This changes what each gate decides, which is why it took a full adversarial cycle rather than one round.

## Blocking grounds raised and cleared

1. The proposed value pattern was itself an enumeration: it could not read a qualified verdict, so such a line was invisible rather than conflicting and #424 survived the fix unchanged. A planned test asserted that line "stays unmatched", pinning the hole open.
2. The target field's parsing was excluded in one unmeasured clause; 62 of 84 reports would still have aborted, changing which finding code printed and nothing else.
3. The claim that nothing emits these forms was false. Two templates emit both forms per report and have drifted from each other.
4. The label probe was itself case-anchored, so a lowercase label was invisible to the reader and to the guard meant to catch what the reader cannot parse. The gate returned true on a report whose stated verdict was a veto.
5. A headline count measured parses and was reported as agreements; the script producing it reproduced the very backtick-capture defect it was measuring.
6. Agreement-required was applied to one field and not the other, leaving first-match selection on a field where a stale report can pass the interdiction.
7. The fix for ground 6 reproduced ground 6: the new field did not get the message contract the first field had, so a contested field reported as absent.
8. A discrimination claim was measured over a 62-report subset and asserted over the 204-report corpus. Measured correctly it was the stronger claim.

## Verified properties

The guard is strictly wider than the reader at every position, so no readable verdict line can escape it; independently fuzzed over 60,000 inputs with zero counterexamples. Every malformed qualifier shape fails closed. The `value is None` contract holds on both consumer paths. Both modules were swept for remaining field selections and none exist. Every count in the plan names the population it was measured over.

## Limits

The reviewer executed the patterns and the corpus measurements but no implementation exists yet, so nothing here verifies the code. Three findings were characterisation and citation accuracy rather than mechanism. Two adjacent defects were filed rather than folded into scope: the gate whose abort produced no observable effect across a run of sealed phases, and two gate artifacts recording a wrong target, one as an absolute local path. The template convergence that is the root cause is deferred with its issue filed, because the historical corpus must be readable in both forms permanently regardless.
